JUCE patch: let an app switch off the macOS window-order check in ComponentPeer hit testing.

Why: JUCE decides which component a mouse event reaches with ComponentPeer::contains(), and on macOS that asks
the window server whether this window is the topmost one at the point. A window behind another window (or
another app) therefore never receives an event, even a synthetic one. The app's in-app test mode
(--automation) drives its own windows by script and must not depend on, nor change, the window order on the
user's screen. This patch adds the process-wide flag juce::ComponentPeer::ignoreWindowOrderForHitTests
(default false) and makes NSViewComponentPeer::contains() skip the window-order check while it is true.
Nothing else changes; with the flag false JUCE behaves exactly as stock.

Applied by cmake/ApplyJucePatch.cmake (FetchContent PATCH_COMMAND); mechanism and how to update it for a new
JUCE tag: docs/development/juce-patches.md. The JUCE files use CRLF line endings.

diff --git a/modules/juce_gui_basics/native/juce_NSViewComponentPeer_mac.mm b/modules/juce_gui_basics/native/juce_NSViewComponentPeer_mac.mm
index ed9cd36..22726a1 100644
--- a/modules/juce_gui_basics/native/juce_NSViewComponentPeer_mac.mm
+++ b/modules/juce_gui_basics/native/juce_NSViewComponentPeer_mac.mm
@@ -529,7 +529,7 @@ bool contains (Point<int> localPos, bool trueIfInAChildWindow) const override
             && isPositiveAndBelow (localPos.getY(), viewFrame.size.height)))
             return false;
 
-        if (! SystemStats::isRunningInAppExtensionSandbox())
+        if (! SystemStats::isRunningInAppExtensionSandbox() && ! ignoreWindowOrderForHitTests)
         {
             if (NSWindow* const viewWindow = [view window])
             {
diff --git a/modules/juce_gui_basics/windows/juce_ComponentPeer.h b/modules/juce_gui_basics/windows/juce_ComponentPeer.h
index b39b604..e133acc 100644
--- a/modules/juce_gui_basics/windows/juce_ComponentPeer.h
+++ b/modules/juce_gui_basics/windows/juce_ComponentPeer.h
@@ -458,6 +458,11 @@ public:
     */
     static bool isValidPeer (const ComponentPeer* peer) noexcept;
 
+    /** When true, the macOS peer's contains() no longer asks the window server whether another window
+        covers the point, so a window that is behind others (or behind another app) still hit-tests as
+        its own. Set once at startup by an app's automation mode; false (stock behaviour) otherwise. */
+    static inline bool ignoreWindowOrderForHitTests = false;
+
     //==============================================================================
     virtual StringArray getAvailableRenderingEngines() = 0;
     virtual int getCurrentRenderingEngine() const;
